WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.968
-We are honored to have
our first guest with us tonight.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:08.767
He served for 36 years
as a senator from Delaware.

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:11.834
He was Vice President
under the Obama Administration,

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:16.334
and now he serves as the 46th
President of the United States.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.200
This is his first time
on a late night program

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.534
as the sitting president.

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:23.100
Please welcome
President Joe Biden!

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:26.300
[ The Roots play
"Hail to the Chief" ]

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.334
[ Laughs ] Yes!

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:30.167
-Hey, Jimmy.
How are you, man?

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:32.868
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:35.167
President Biden,
I appreciate you being here.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.968
It's your first time on our show
as President Biden,

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:39.701
and I'm honored.

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:42.467
-I'm honored to be on.
Thanks for inviting me.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.367
-We have lots to talk about.

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.133
Let's start with
some good news here.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:49.167
You passed
your infrastructure bill.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.133
This is a big deal.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:53.501
Passed!

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:54.767
What are some changes

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:57.667
that Americans can expect
from passing the bill?

00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:00.467
-Well, you know, we used to be
the number one,

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.133
have the best infrastructure
in the world --

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:05.133
highways, bridges,
the whole works.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:08.601
And now we rank number 13
in the world.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.634
And that has a lot
to do with quality of life.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.734
It has a lot to do
with whether or not

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:15.000
we're going to be competitive.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.634
For example,
one thing it does --

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:19.601
we're going to replace
all the lead pipes in America

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:22.567
that are causing people
to get sick, get cancer,

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:25.367
and kids to be able
to drink clean water.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.267
We're going to make sure
that we have

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:31.133
everywhere in the country,
rural and urban and suburban,

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.634
we have Internet connections.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.367
Because the world is changing,

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:36.067
and we're so far
behind the curve.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.367
But the big thing
it's going to do,

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.367
it's going to create
millions of jobs,

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.234
and it's going to change
the quality of life

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.033
for an awful lot of people
around the country.

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.133
-Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:47.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's great.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.167
And I know you've been
working hard

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:52.100
on the Build Back Better Plan.
-Yes.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.534
-Some people may not
fully understand

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:55.534
what's actually in this plan.

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:57.601
Is there a simple way
to break it down?

00:01:57.601 --> 00:01:59.801
-Yeah.
What's in it is the ability

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:02.300
for working class
and middle class people

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.000
to have the cost of living
cut significantly.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.968
For example, there's money
in there to make sure

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:10.934
that there is the ability
to care for childcare.

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:12.801
Right now,
if you're in New York

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:14.767
and you're a man or a woman

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.601
having childcare
for your children,

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:21.167
you're paying $21,000 to $25,000
a year to be able to do that.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:22.767
Well, most people can't do that,

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:24.701
so people leave the work force.

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:28.334
This will mean you don't have to
pay more than 7% of your income,

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:31.601
saving tens of thousands
of dollars over time.

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:36.067
We also provided an ability,
Build Back Better Initiative,

00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:37.934
we're going to make sure
you're able to send

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:40.734
your 3- and 4- and 5-year-olds
to school,

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:42.267
which will increase
exponentially

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:43.901
their chance of succeeding.

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.534
All of the studies show, Jimmy,

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:48.801
that 47% better chance
of graduating from high school,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.067
no matter what the background
you come from,

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:53.300
no matter what home
you come from,

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.167
and to be able to go on
to get to school.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:57.567
What better can happen
for America

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:59.267
than have a better
educated population?

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:00.634
-Absolutely.

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.634
-There's a whole range
of things that are in there

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:05.100
that are going to really reduce,
essentially,

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:09.534
the cost of living for people
in a reasonable, rational way.

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:14.067
And by the way, every single bit
of that bill is paid for.

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:16.601
No one making
less than $400,000 a year

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:20.667
will pay
an additional cent in taxes,

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:25.534
as well as it will not increase
the deficit one penny.

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:29.767
-Do you think this will pass
the Senate before the year?

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:31.200
-Well, I hope it will.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.667
I don't have a single Republican
vote right now to pass it.

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:36.167
And, uh --
-Wow!

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:39.467
-So, it's going to be tough,
but I think we can get it done.

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:41.934
If we don't get it, I'm going to
keep at it until we get it done.

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.968
-I was at the Kennedy Center,

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:47.968
and I saw Republicans
and Democrats in the crowd.

00:03:47.968 --> 00:03:51.234
Everyone was laughing at jokes
and listening to great music.

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:53.901
And everyone seemed
cordial and nice.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:56.934
And I go, "This seems like
this should be much easier

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.701
to get along with everybody."

00:03:58.701 --> 00:03:59.868
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:03.501
[ Laughter ]
-Well, Jimmy, look,

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:08.367
the truth is
that before COVID hit,

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:12.901
the Trump arm
of the Republican Party,

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:16.834
which seems to be
the Republican Party now,

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:19.267
did not even show up
at the Kennedy Center.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:21.067
They wouldn't go to the awards.

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:24.567
So all the people you have
that we saw at that event,

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:27.100
which was a very fulsome event,

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.334
were people who in fact
are Republicans,

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:32.234
but they're the kind --
like for example,

00:04:32.234 --> 00:04:33.901
a lot of Republicans
and Democrats

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:35.667
used to get
really on well together.

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:36.767
For example, one of the reasons

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:38.734
I was a little bit late
coming on

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:42.133
is because -- not coming on,
but to do the taping here,

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:45.534
is because
I did Bob Dole's eulogy today.

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:48.467
He asked me on his deathbed
whether I would do his eulogy.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:51.467
We were friends. We disagreed,
but we were friends.

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:53.868
We used to have an awful lot
of that relationship,

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:57.400
and it still exists,
except that the Qanon

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.701
and the extreme elements
of the Republican Party

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:03.968
and what Donald Trump
keeps sort of, seems to me,

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:08.467
feeding, you know,
with the big lie,

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:09.834
it makes it awful hard.

00:05:09.834 --> 00:05:13.567
And I think most Republicans --

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:15.400
there's an awful lot
of Republicans in Congress

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.801
I think would agree with that.

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:21.067
-Yeah, I thought it was great
to see you there.

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:23.501
We gave you a standing ovation
because I go, "Here he is.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:26.434
He's bringing class back.
He's a classy guy."

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:28.400
And you're bringing class
back to the office.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.033
-You're very kind to say that.
-And I thought it was amazing

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:32.801
that you did that.
-Thank you.

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:34.834
-The COVID problem.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.334
I don't know what else to do,

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:40.267
and how to tell people
to get the vaccine.

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:42.100
At this point, I think people
are going to do

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.334
what they will, I guess.

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:44.634
I don't know what to say.

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:48.100
Is it the youth
that we have to hope

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.334
the kids get us out of this?

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:51.434
Because, I mean, I got vaxxed,
I got boosted,

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.334
I got whatever you got.

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:54.934
If you want me to wear
red pants,

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:55.968
I'll wear red pants.

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:58.300
I want this thing to go away.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.968
-Well, I think what we ought
to do is have more people

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:01.567
listen to your song.

00:06:01.567 --> 00:06:03.400
-Yeah that's what
I'm talking about, yeah.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.868
[ Applause ]

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:06.501
-I think that will
get them moving.

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:10.934
-I gotta tell you --
So I had this song come out,

00:06:10.934 --> 00:06:13.501
it's called "It Was
a Masked Christmas" this week,

00:06:13.501 --> 00:06:16.901
with Ariana Grande
and Megan Thee Stallion, and --

00:06:16.901 --> 00:06:18.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:22.601
You were nice enough
to tweet about it --

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:24.267
"'Tis the season
(to get boosted)."

00:06:24.267 --> 00:06:27.634
This is amazing
that the president did this.

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:30.734
I am so excited
that you did this.

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:31.767
It changed everything.

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:33.901
All these radio stations
want the song.

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:36.434
Now they're playing the song.

00:06:36.434 --> 00:06:38.334
But you said
in another comment,

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:40.601
you said the message
is very important --

00:06:40.601 --> 00:06:42.501
get your booster.

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.367
-Well, it is.
It's really important, Jimmy.

00:06:44.367 --> 00:06:48.000
Look, we're so far ahead
of the rest of the world

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.901
in terms
of the science and technology

00:06:49.901 --> 00:06:51.667
to produce the vaccines.

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:54.133
And now we found out that

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:58.334
if you have your two shots
for Moderna or from Pfizer

00:06:58.334 --> 00:07:02.400
or the one shot from J&amp;J,
what happens is,

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.934
this booster shot

00:07:03.934 --> 00:07:07.100
not only brings
the levels back up of immunity,

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:10.067
I mean, to deal with fighting
off the virus,

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:11.534
any of the viruses,

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:14.033
but it brings it up
exponentially.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:16.567
So if you want to be sure
you're going to be okay --

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:18.167
And the other good news, Jimmy,

00:07:18.167 --> 00:07:21.601
is that we now have
5-, 6-, and 7-year-olds

00:07:21.601 --> 00:07:25.167
are able to be vaccinated,
as well as teenagers.

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:27.701
And so we're moving.
We're moving.

00:07:27.701 --> 00:07:31.267
Now, I don't,
the politicalization of this,

00:07:31.267 --> 00:07:33.968
making it become
a political statement

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:36.834
if you get the shot and somehow,
I don't know what the h--

00:07:36.834 --> 00:07:39.167
Anyway.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.167 --> 00:07:44.033
Here's the deal, Jimmy.

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:50.400
The bottom line is that the way
to avoid this virus

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.601
is to get two shots
and then get the booster shot.

00:07:54.601 --> 00:07:57.734
It's available.
We have the medicines available.

00:07:57.734 --> 00:07:59.934
It will make
a gigantic difference.

00:07:59.934 --> 00:08:02.400
And even if you don't care
so much about yourself,

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:03.667
think about your kids,
your brother,

00:08:03.667 --> 00:08:05.968
your sister, your co-worker.

00:08:05.968 --> 00:08:08.033
And this stuff about Biden

00:08:08.033 --> 00:08:09.834
is mandating
these things happening

00:08:09.834 --> 00:08:11.968
and it's un-American,

00:08:11.968 --> 00:08:13.100
look at it this way --

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.534
it's patriotic to get this done.

00:08:15.534 --> 00:08:16.667
Not a joke.

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:19.133
It's patriotic to get it done.
-Yeah.

00:08:19.133 --> 00:08:23.100
Do you, um, how much do you pay
attention to approval ratings?

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.334
-Well, not anymore.

00:08:25.334 --> 00:08:26.601
I'm joking.

00:08:26.601 --> 00:08:29.400
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.234
I was paying attention
when it was in the mid 60s.

00:08:32.234 --> 00:08:34.667
Now I'm in the mid 40s,
I don't pay attention.

00:08:34.667 --> 00:08:37.100
-I appreciate the honesty,
yeah.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:40.200
I mean, because you came in --
you came in hot.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.133
And then you got to medium,
but now you're at a low.

00:08:43.133 --> 00:08:44.467
But you've just got to keep
your head down, right,

00:08:44.467 --> 00:08:46.467
and just keep
doing the right thing?

00:08:46.467 --> 00:08:47.968
-Well, look, here's the deal.

00:08:47.968 --> 00:08:52.501
I think that it's --
We've been in less than a year.

00:08:52.501 --> 00:08:53.934
A lot has happened.

00:08:53.934 --> 00:08:55.400
And look, people are afraid.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.901
People are worried.

00:08:56.901 --> 00:09:02.200
And people are getting so much
inaccurate information to them.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:05.667
I don't mean about me,
but about the situation.

00:09:05.667 --> 00:09:10.767
And so, you know, they're being
told that, you know,

00:09:10.767 --> 00:09:12.601
Armageddon is on the way.

00:09:12.601 --> 00:09:15.434
The truth is, the economy
is growing more than it has

00:09:15.434 --> 00:09:17.701
any time in close to 60 years.

00:09:17.701 --> 00:09:20.133
The unemployment rate
is down to 4.2%.

00:09:20.133 --> 00:09:22.167
It's going to go lower,
in my view.

00:09:22.167 --> 00:09:23.868
We do have inflation on things

00:09:23.868 --> 00:09:26.701
that in fact matter
to people's lives.

00:09:26.701 --> 00:09:28.334
You know, when you show up
at a gas station

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:30.934
and it's $3.50 at your pump,

00:09:30.934 --> 00:09:36.400
although now because
I took 50 million barrels,

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:39.868
I called the oil petroleum
reserve,

00:09:39.868 --> 00:09:42.334
the gasoline is down below $3
in many places.

00:09:42.334 --> 00:09:43.701
It's going to come down.

00:09:43.701 --> 00:09:44.901
It's going to move.

00:09:44.901 --> 00:09:46.801
But in the meantime,
people are worried.

00:09:46.801 --> 00:09:49.567
And they're worried about
whether or not

00:09:49.567 --> 00:09:51.968
they have a brother,
sister, uncle, aunt

00:09:51.968 --> 00:09:53.434
who has gotten COVID,

00:09:53.434 --> 00:09:54.968
and they don't know
what to do about it.

00:09:54.968 --> 00:09:57.434
I mean, so there is
a lot of anxiety,

00:09:57.434 --> 00:10:00.067
and my job is to be
straightforward,

00:10:00.067 --> 00:10:01.534
shoot from the shoulder,

00:10:01.534 --> 00:10:04.100
let people know exactly
what the truth is,

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:08.000
and lay out how I'm going to try
to make life better for them.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.701
-Yeah. Does anyone really
understand how hard your job is?

00:10:12.701 --> 00:10:16.434
Like, who, I mean --
besides my uncle, apparently,

00:10:16.434 --> 00:10:18.367
who knows everything.

00:10:18.367 --> 00:10:20.033
He knows everything.
But I mean --

00:10:20.033 --> 00:10:21.300
-Well, send him over.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.801
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.801 --> 00:10:25.167
-Yeah, no, you don't
want to talk to this guy.

00:10:25.167 --> 00:10:26.567
[ Laughter ]

00:10:26.567 --> 00:10:29.501
But I mean, even just being
in D.C. the other day

00:10:29.501 --> 00:10:30.734
and driving around,

00:10:30.734 --> 00:10:32.701
you see all these giant
buildings and you just --

00:10:32.701 --> 00:10:34.868
you feel kind of nervous
and you feel like --

00:10:34.868 --> 00:10:36.300
I feel important when I'm there,

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:38.968
but you're the leader
of our country.

00:10:38.968 --> 00:10:40.634
I mean, the pressure.

00:10:40.634 --> 00:10:43.534
And then you have to do
20 events

00:10:43.534 --> 00:10:45.367
during the day
that we don't even see.

00:10:45.367 --> 00:10:48.033
-Well, look, I was
Vice President for eight years.

00:10:48.033 --> 00:10:50.601
I knew what the job was,
and I don't --

00:10:50.601 --> 00:10:52.100
no one should feel sorry for me.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.968
It's the greatest honor anybody
can have in their whole life,

00:10:54.968 --> 00:10:56.767
in my view, is to be
President of the United States.

00:10:56.767 --> 00:10:59.868
But what the difference is --

00:10:59.868 --> 00:11:04.400
the difference is that
when you're in Congress --

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.801
and I had important jobs
in the Congress as a senator.

00:11:06.801 --> 00:11:09.167
I was chairman
of important committees.

00:11:09.167 --> 00:11:11.267
But being President is like
being chairman

00:11:11.267 --> 00:11:13.067
of every single committee.

00:11:13.067 --> 00:11:17.100
Nothing gets to my desk unless
it hasn't been able to be solved

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.801
before it got to my desk.

00:11:18.801 --> 00:11:21.367
So by definition,
it's more difficult.

00:11:21.367 --> 00:11:23.467
Harry Truman had a great line.

00:11:23.467 --> 00:11:27.434
He said about being president,
he said, "The buck stops here."

00:11:27.434 --> 00:11:29.767
I used to be -- I kid at Barack,

00:11:29.767 --> 00:11:31.901
President Obama,
who was a good friend

00:11:31.901 --> 00:11:34.534
and we served eight years
as friends together.

00:11:34.534 --> 00:11:37.534
And I used to say to him --
instead of him thanking me,

00:11:37.534 --> 00:11:39.901
I got to be the last guy
in the room to give him advice.

00:11:39.901 --> 00:11:41.467
That was the deal we had.

00:11:41.467 --> 00:11:44.601
And he'd thank me, and I get
to walk out and say, "Look,

00:11:44.601 --> 00:11:47.000
I give you the advice,
you got to make the decision."

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:49.601
-Yeah.
-"And, you know, what happens

00:11:49.601 --> 00:11:51.200
is going to be on you."

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:52.701
But that's part of the deal.

00:11:52.701 --> 00:11:55.634
But look, I have
enormous confidence --

00:11:55.634 --> 00:12:00.834
You're going to realize
what a naive guy I am.

00:12:00.834 --> 00:12:04.234
But I really have faith
at the end of the day

00:12:04.234 --> 00:12:06.267
the American people
are going to get it.

00:12:06.267 --> 00:12:08.667
They understand.
They understand.

00:12:08.667 --> 00:12:11.701
Given half a shot,
they have never, ever, ever,

00:12:11.701 --> 00:12:13.300
ever let the country down.

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:15.701
We've just to give them a shot.
-That's right.

00:12:15.701 --> 00:12:18.968
More with President Joe Biden
when we come back, everybody.

